    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Hello, and welcome to Why Is This Happening With Me, your host, Chris Hayes. Well, it's a snow day here in the beautiful Northeast. I did some sledding with my kids. I hope wherever you are as you're preparing for the holidays or enjoying the holidays, you are safe and sound and warm and by some kind of hearth with people you love, but not too many people you love indoors, of course, because this is the COVID winter. You know we've been on the podcast and on the show and actually in some writing that I've been doing for myself really just trying to sort of like work through what happened in this election because it was there was so much build up to it it was such a strange election in some ways it was a complicated election in which I think there was a bunch of different messages that kind of went in different directions. And so, for me, as someone who does this for a living and really tries to think through the forensics after an election, to be really rigorous and clear out about what didn't happen and the many different stories one could tell to try to get a better and clearer sense of where American politics are at, We're going to continue on that theme today. We've talked to Debbie Mukhersel Powell, of course, who is a representative from Miami-Dade in Florida. She won in 2018 and then lost now ranked in 2020. Talk to David Shor, who is a consultant and work data scientist who works with polling and super PACs in trying to get Democrats elected. And today, a rare repeat guest on the program. We tend not to repeat guests. We've had a few, my wife, Kate Shaw, is in that Augusta category. But today, a rare sequel, which is the Congressman from the 11th District in New York, which is all of Staten Island and parts of Brooklyn, a guy by the name of Max Rose, he was on our program before, because He's got a fascinating story in history. He ran a very, very good race in 2018 and defeated a Republican incumbent in that race and then lost this time around in a district that was a difficult district. Everyone knew it would be a frontline district. And so, as with Debbie Mookersill-Powell, I thought rather than going to the pundits are looking at big aggregate polling data. One of the best ways to sort of find out what was happening on the ground in this election in various different places is to go to people that ran those races. And so it's a great pleasure to have Congressman Max Rose back in the program. How you doing?",
