    "turn_idx": 39,
    "turn_text": "It's absolutely hard to do. I got more aggregate votes than any Democrat in the history of my district to include President Obama and President-elect Biden. But it was not enough. But then an entirely separate question is why did we so in so many congressional districts so significantly underperformed Joe Biden? And that is a question about the branding of the party. That is a question about trust. And that is also a question of did we stay at home too much? Did we not get out there? Were we not physically aggressive when it comes to canvassing and pushing forward a proactive message? But to say that there's just one question in this conversation, I think doesn't do this issue justice.",
