  {
    "episode_id": 72856,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72856.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 40,
    "turn_text": "Right. Well, so let me, I mean, one of the reasons I want to talk to you is because there has been so much You know, there's been so much made of the aftermath of the Georgia Floyd protests and then defund the police. And it just occurred to me, you know, every district's different and there's a bunch of different things that are happening in different places. You know, the one place in America where you could say, yeah, that might have cost the Democrat the seat is your district, honestly, because it's like, you know, it is a district that has tons of, both current and retired police, A, B, it's like a very, you know, it's politics. I think are even people that aren't police, I think particularly the white folks, although not exclusively in that district, they don't really don't like to see images of people breaking down windows and things like that. And then last of all, I would say that, I watched the ads and like clearly your opponent, that was what she ran on. I mean, you know, in other races, I sort of feel like people are kind of casting about for reasons that don't line up with the data. I do feel like in your race, you know, that that was pretty clearly pretty top of mind. But I guess what's your feeling about it?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The aftermath of the George Floyd protests and 'defund the police' movement has received significant attention.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
