    "turn_text": "Look, I, first of all, Chris, I got nothing to lose, politically speaking. So I'm not going to tap dance around any issue here, or ever. First of all, to your original point, yes, like I do consider it my responsibility to be present for communities and to hear people out. But with that being said, though, I am a supporter of police reform. And I'm not going to shy away from that. I was a co-sponsor of the Justice and Policing Act, and I do think that there were reforms necessary. The point that I'm trying to make is I don't think that's in conflict with believing that the majority of police officers are heroes who are doing the trying, their hardest to do the right thing. We just can't then say, oh, this is just a bad apple situation. There are systems that we have got to reform. You know, it's fascinating, man. Like, after this election, I got people like Tanya has to code say, well, Max, whatever happens with Max Rose, you know, that's Max Rose's problem. Why does that affect what I'm saying? Like, he's right. Like, no one should shut up because I lost, like, have vibrant conversations. But if we're going to have a conversation about police reform and you think defunding is the answer, I think you're monumentally missing.",
