    "turn_text": "I want to, so I want to also talk about, you mentioned COVID someone in passing and right now there's like a, there's a kind of bit of an uprising on Staten Island against COVID restrictions. There's a bar that's staying open in violation of, you know, the city and state orders. I want to talk about the role that played in your election right after we take this quick break. So Max, you mentioned COVID earlier about the fact that the shelter-in-place lockdowns were not popular in Staten Island in your district. And I think there's lots of ways in which, I mean, at one level, right, they're not popular with anyone. I mean, they're not popular with me. Like, I don't want to not do fun things outside. But there's a deeper way in which they got viewed as this kind of is sort of out of touch technocratic liberal tyranny over people trying to live their lives. I just wonder how much that you felt that was a factor in the race.",
