    "turn_idx": 73,
    "turn_text": "It should drive you insane because it's relatively simple. On the same hand, what I'm talking about here is trying to show sensitivity towards pain. I was one of the early advocates for opening up indoor dining, for instance. What we've heard so much over the last nine months is, well, we have to listen to the scientists. We have to listen to the scientists. People were saying it all over TV. And of course, how could you disagree with that? We have to listen to the scientists. But here's the thing that scientists are not doing, is they're not balancing interests. And this is a difficult thing to talk about, right? Because like here I am trying to peel the layers on this, but if you just say we're listening to scientists, right? And you're saying that as a politician, are you then abdicating what is your duty to balance interests against each other, to balance the interests of economic well-being and public health and so on and so forth? So that's one element that I think there was a bit of a language problem",
