  {
    "episode_id": 72856,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72856.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 75,
    "turn_text": "But yeah, you just don't want to ever seem like you're abdicating your duty. But I actually think we should reverse the conversation on COVID, which is like COVID was not a winner for the Republicans. By any sense of the word from a political standpoint, it just wasn't. And so the deeper question here is not how was, how did the Republicans successfully and politically leverage COVID? I don't think they did. I think that they handled it, they underestimated it, they mocked it, they started funding. So like the deeper point here is in the absence of COVID, how much worse could a democratic loss have been? Right. It's not like the Republicans shouldn't be looking at each other right now and say, man, we really got this COVID messaging correct. They didn't get the policy correct, they didn't get the messaging correct, they didn't get the science correct, and they certainly didn't help unify the country. What's scary is all hell though, is that they still nearly want, despite that, not because of it.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
