    "turn_text": "ever if I was a baseball player. So, but what I do believe is that because you have one party, the Democratic Party, that is proactive in nature, that its entire DNA is centered around how can we be proactive to make America better and your life better using the arm of government to do so versus a Republican Party, which is and labels itself as conservative. i.e. our first impulse would be not to do things, even in the face of suffering and injustice. When you have that type of dichotomy, it will always be harder for Democrats to win elections than Republicans. So like, how often do you hear from Democrats talking about Republicans, oh, man, I don't understand how they can get away with this. Why can they do that? It's constant inferiority complex, like just wondering why they can do something we can't. Well, damn it, because our agendas are different. And let's just embrace the fact that it is harder to do things to win elections as a Democrat. As a consequence, I do think that Democrats have to do two things. And I say this again, humbly as someone who just came off on a loss, so take it or leave it. I think one is that there has to be an over investment in trust building, which comes, you know, humans are naturally irrational creatures. And trust building is not, you know, do that with a policy document. And you know, you can't do that quickly. And secondly, there has to be an investment in bold simplicity. And one of the biggest problems in the Democratic Party right now is that there seems to be this unnecessary clash, ideologically speaking, between quote-unquote progressives who claim that they have the mantle of boldness and moderates who do not. I think that the Democratic Party has to do away with that and become the party of bold simplicity and try to find unity around that. And when you over invest in those two things, bold simplicity and trust building, I think that we can consistently win elections knowing that it will always be harder for us to win than Republicans who only have to vilify us.",
