    "turn_text": "are all things that we can end reembracing this notion that we are the party against forever wars. We are the party against unnecessary military efforts. like that. And we lost that in an age of trouble. We're like, we became so reflexively anti-Trump that even when this dude wants to get out of Afghanistan, suddenly we become the party that says we're pro-stained in Afghanistan forever. Like we lost our identity. He becomes pro-tariff, so now we become the party of neoliberalism. It doesn't make any sense. So I do think that we have to go back to a North Star here. of being on the side of the working class, being on the side of those who can't afford to influence the political process with the strength of their pocketbooks. And in that sense, it's a moral, inclusive populism that I can unify the party.",
