    "turn_idx": 108,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, no, I've hit like pretty big IEDs and gotten like relatively exorbitantly, like relatively messed up from that. I've, what hurt more than that was watching people I love. And I was entrusted with leading get hurt in combat. That's something that I'll never be able to kick. This, like, loosing sucks, and your name's on the ballot, and it hurts. And anyone who tells you that it doesn't hurt is really lying. And it's so funny, like, you come back to Washington, D.C., and no one can say the right thing to you. I go, one colleague comes up to me and they acknowledge my loss. And I'm like, you insensitive prick, don't you know I just had this conversation 30 seconds ago? And then another colleague comes up to me and they don't acknowledge my loss. And I'm like, you insensitive prick, why are you acting like nothing happened? So I get it. But what And by the way, man, to all of your listeners, if you're talking to someone who just lost an election, don't remind them that Barack Obama lost a race for Congress and then went on to do great",
