  {
    "episode_id": 72856,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72856.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 113,
    "turn_text": "funny. It's either Abe Lincoln or Barack Obama. They lost this and that. One door shuts, another door opens. Just shut up, shut up. It doesn't help. And then you just kind of have to bounce back. Like it's because for all the ways in which, like losing them, and this is going to sound like kind of cliche, but it's the truth. Like if your only commitment to public service rests around not getting defeated or not taking a loss. Then you probably didn't deserve to be there in the first place. And if you weren't willing to risk it all, which I did a few times, and I'm proud that I risked everything to do what I felt was right. Everyone says that, but to actually do it, I'm proud of that. I mean, I would say I've been broken up with an IED and I've lost an election. I still think getting broken up with hurts the most.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
