    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72856.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 124,
    "turn_text": "It's hard. And it's something that, you know, I really want to work on to, you know, be present and to be able to compartmentalize and to understand that the haters can't take a pound of flesh out of you. People I think often forget that Our system is filled with human beings. And if there's anything I've learned in Congress in my first couple of years, and maybe my only couple of years in Congress, is that while all politics is local, all congressional politics is personal. And the second that you forget that these institutions are filled with human beings, I think you will lose sight of really how the institutions operate.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Forgetting that institutions are made of people leads to misunderstanding how they function.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "It is difficult to be present and to compartmentalize emotions.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The political system consists of human individuals rather than abstract entities.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "All congressional politics is personal.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
